<h1>What Is SWP? Systematic Withdrawal Plan Explained Simply</h1>
<p>A plain-language guide from Finvestro.</p>
</section>

<main class="wrap"><article class="info" style="margin-top:0"><p>A SWP, or Systematic Withdrawal Plan, lets you take out a fixed amount from your mutual fund investment at regular intervals, such as every month. The rest of your money stays invested. People often use it to create a regular cash flow, for example after retirement.</p>
<h2>How does a SWP work?</h2>
<p>You choose the amount, the date and the scheme. On each date, the fund sells enough units to pay your amount and sends it to your bank account. The units that remain keep moving up or down with the market.</p>
<h2>A simple example</h2>
<p>Suppose you have ₹50,00,000 invested and withdraw ₹30,000 every month for 15 years, and the investment grows at an assumed 9% a year. You would withdraw ₹54,00,000 in total, and about ₹72 lakh would still be left at the end. This is only an illustration. Real returns can be higher or lower, and the money can run out sooner if returns are low or withdrawals are high. Try your own numbers in our <a href="calculators.html#swp">SWP calculator</a>.</p>
<h2>Who may find it useful</h2>
<p>• People who want a regular income from their savings, such as retirees.<br>• Anyone who wants a regular payout without selling the whole investment at once.</p>
<h2>Things to keep in mind</h2>
<p>• Mutual funds are subject to market risk, and the value of your investment can go down as well as up.<br>• If you withdraw more than the investment earns, the balance will keep falling.<br>• Each withdrawal is a redemption, so tax and exit load may apply. Tax depends on the type of scheme and how long you held the units, so please check with a tax professional.<br>• Review the withdrawal amount once a year.</p>
<h2>SWP and STP: what is the difference?</h2>
<p>An SWP pays money to your bank account. An STP moves money from one scheme to another. You can compare both in our <a href="calculators.html#stp">STP calculator</a>.</p>
<h2>How to start</h2>
<p>Choose the scheme, the monthly amount and the date with the help of your distributor. If you would like help, <a href="index.html#contact">contact us</a> or <a href="https://wa.me/919166646162?text=Hi%20Finvestro%2C%20I%20read%20your%20blog%20and%20would%20like%20to%20talk." target="_blank" rel="noopener">message us on WhatsApp</a>.</p>
